  "limits": "Bin supply contract of the three priority-prefix entries only: the three bin marker routes of each sole caller, the shared tail, the boundary error record and the dl split between the byte-fed entry and the alternate slice decoder. What could set dl nonzero is NOT established by these bytes: both call sites of each decoder pass rdx=0 and no dl-writing instruction sits on the jump-table path, so as wired the byte-fed entry route is the taken one; the alternate decoder (0x2b87440 and its siblings) is not traced. The peeked-marker entry path of the decoder (reader bytes at +0x20/+0x21) and the marker taxonomy beyond the three bin markers are not traced. The caller imposes no payload-length cap beyond the reader remaining count and never inspects the entry count cell; what the entry does with payload bytes past its certified three-byte prefix (the merged packet's optional-suffix question) is not established here. Semantic type names beyond the merged packet's diagnostic label, caller-of-parent provenance and any reconstruction gate are not claimed. No captured code executed."
